  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. The fix is complete and correct.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Bug:** In `src/server/services/member-service.ts` line 94, the `removeMember` function was calling:\n```typescript\nawait assertLastOwnerRetained(input.orgId, input.memberId, \"owner\");\n```\n\nThis passed `\"owner\"` as the `nextRole` parameter, but `assertLastOwnerRetained` has an early return when `nextRole === \"owner\"` (line 132), bypassing the owner count validation entirely.\n\n**Why Demotion Worked:** The `updateMemberRole` function correctly passes the actual target role (like `\"member\"`), which doesn't match the early return condition, so the validation runs and properly prevents demoting the last owner.\n\n**The Fix:** Changed line 94 to pass `\"member\"` instead of `\"owner\"`:\n```typescript\nawait assertLastOwnerRetained(input.orgId, input.memberId, \"member\");\n```\n\nNow both removal and demotion of the last owner are correctly prevented, and the organization cannot be left without an owner.",
